	•	Explainability / Interpretability Used: No
	•	Feature Selection Method: Automated (e.g., LASSO, Stepwise)
	•	Hyperparameter Tuning Reported: Yes
	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper used “in-house three-dimensional (3-D) convolutional neural networks (CNN) algorithms” based on U-Net to segment recipient lungs and chest cavity from CT. The actual DCC prediction model was a multivariate logistic regression using preoperative features, with backward stepwise elimination and stratified 5-fold cross-validation. Because ML/CNN was used mainly for imaging-derived measurement extraction rather than the primary predictive model, Primary ML Component is best classified as Other. No SHAP/LIME-style interpretability was reported.  ￼

