	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The methods state that variables with “less than 5% missing data were imputed using mean or mode imputation,” while variables with more than 5% missingness were excluded. Continuous features were z-score standardized, categorical variables were one-hot encoded, and VIF filtering plus backward elimination were applied. The model used stratified 5-fold cross-validation rather than a single explicit train/test split, so fixed training/test counts are NR. No class-imbalance method or code-release statement was reported.  ￼

