Section 6: Quality Assessment (Risk of Bias / PROBAST)
	•	Participants (Selection Bias): High Risk | Quote/Reasoning: This was a small, highly selected single-center cohort of only 92 systemic sclerosis recipients, which limits generalizability.  ￼
	•	Predictors (Input Variable Bias): Low Risk | Quote/Reasoning: Predictors were clinically relevant preoperative variables plus objectively derived CT volumetric measures from validated CNN algorithms.  ￼
	•	Outcome (Definition Bias): Low Risk | Quote/Reasoning: The outcome, DCC vs PCC, was clearly defined intraoperatively, and survival outcomes were assessed with Kaplan–Meier analysis at prespecified time points.  ￼
	•	Analysis (Modeling Bias): Unclear | Quote/Reasoning: Strengths include CT-derived quantitative metrics, cross-validation, hyperparameter tuning, and multivariable modeling; uncertainty remains because of the small sample size, single-center design, and lack of external validation.  ￼
	•	Applicability to Review Question: Low Concern | Quote/Reasoning: The paper directly concerns lung transplantation, uses deep-learning-derived CT measurements, and addresses a clinically meaningful perioperative transplant outcome.  ￼

